                                                "sense_id": "7fc37d46-f841-3d44-87e3-66cfac10c6f9",
                                                "text": "It should be obvious by now that most of what goes on in the Bulova commercial does not depend very much on an appeal to the rational part of the mind—the “logos” of Aristotle. If it were to depend on such an appeal to the reason, it might show the same woman, but dressed sensibly in a nice buttoned-up dress and wearing her glasses."
